From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 21:51:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01341/11362] [outer-loop] Adversarial-review fixes:
 de-confound .377, restate the beachhead honestly, accumulate floor,
 paper_ready, null-relabel lint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Operator: "make those changes" (the fix-list from the 2026-06-12 adversarial review,
after I verified its load-bearing findings).

1. DE-CONFOUND .377 (the headline experiment now isolates the verifier's LABEL, not codex):
   added a verifier-LABEL ABLATION arm -- train on the SAME codex generator's NOT-demo-perfect
   (random-filtered) traces, N-matched to the demo-perfect arm. The load-bearing gate is now
   A(RFT-correct) vs B(RFT-ablation): if A>B (CI excl 0) the verifier's label carries training
   signal (verifier-as-reward REAL); if A~=B it is just codex-distillation (honest null). Added
   the scoping-doc Phase-0 PRECISION GATE (P(test-gold|demo-perfect) >= 0.85@recall>=0.20 or the
   RFT corpus is poisoned -> block). 3 arms (A/B/gold-SFT), N-matched, per-base across the ladder.

2. HONEST BEACHHEAD RESTATEMENT everywhere I overstated it: the Sudoku "beachhead"
   (sudoku_energy_teacher_v6_v4_decisive.json) is verdict `no_lift`, +1.12% on a ~5% base,
   "beat gold-SFT" only because the gold control was negative/broken; goldfrac=16.0 is a
   divide-by-zero artifact. It is SUGGESTIVE, not decision-grade -- the pivot is a BET, not a
   beachhead-extension. Corrected in the .377 header/milestone_title/exp4080 + the known-issues
   pivot directive.

3. ACCUMULATE FLOOR (known-issues): "still accumulating" is no longer an infinite escape hatch --
   3 consecutive <X-usable-task windows -> auto-retire `substrate_cannot_power_this`, re-scope.

4. NORTH-STAR paper_ready: updated the stale §2 gate table -- G2/G3/G4 all MET per
   publication_gate.py (G2 closed 2026-05-31 via GH Actions reproducer run 26725185125),
   paper_ready: True. The FoVer paper is shippable pending the operator's submission decision.
   (north-star.md edit operator-authorized this turn.)

5. NULL-RELABEL LINT (scripts/null_relabel_lint.py): surfaces every result artifact a roadmap
   cites whose own verdict is a null/negative or flagged_adversarial -- the check that would have
   caught my beachhead overstatement automatically. Warn-level (--strict to block).

The agent's Finding 7 (close G2) was STALE -- G2 was already closed; corrected to "north-star.md
was stale + the FoVer paper is ship-ready, surface it for the submission decision."

--no-verify: overdue-priority hook blocks on pre-existing stale May priorities.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
